    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0499" n="1129" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1129"/>

                <head>No. 472.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_RB1"
                            type="from">Beardsley</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Agency
                                and Consulate-General of the United States of America at Alexandria,
                                Egypt</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Cairo</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1873-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 25, 1873</date>. (Received March 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report at this late day
                    that the United States sloop of war Hartford arrived at Port Saïd on the 8th
                    ultimo, and sailed from Suez for China on the 18th ultimo. I presume Mr.
                        <persName>Page</persName> has already reported the arrival and departure of
                    the Hartford, as well as the particulars of her passage through the canal. As
                    Mr. <persName>Page</persName> does not-send his dispatches through this office,
                    I deem it prudent, even at this date, to report the Hartford’s movements, that
                    there may be no doubt of the information having been communicated to the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_RB1">R. BEARDSLEY</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
